@scene(60, 5)

// Threads as relief: a thread is a MACHINING OPERATION, so the geometry is
// the part before it — at its maximum material condition — and the thread is
// a displacement height on the part's material that only the renderer reads.
//
//   the screw   an M6 x 20 socket head cap screw. The geometry is the smooth
//               shank at the major diameter, fastener.shcs; thread.maleRelief
//               takes the ISO 68-1 thread off it on screen.
//   the plate   an M6 hole. The geometry is the bore at the basic MINOR
//               diameter, and thread.femaleRelief taps it.
//   the joint   the two together, the screw backed out six millimetres so
//               its thread shows going into the hole. As designed they
//               INTERFERE, by the annulus between the two diameters over the
//               length they share: that overlap is the thread engagement.
//               Displaced, the flanks meet.
//
// The mesher, every export and every proof see the geometry — the smooth
// screw and the plain bore — and the section plane cuts it as built, so it
// shows the interference the render resolves. That is the point: one object
// is both the form to prove against and the form to look at.
//
// Each relief is bounded, so a part wears ONE material and the thread stops
// where it should: under the head, at the tip, at the mouth of the hole.

steelMat, steelColor = metal.steel();
aluminumMat, aluminumColor = metal.aluminum();

d = 6.0;
pitchVal = thread.metricPitch(d);
screwLength = 20.0;
plateT = 8.0;

// The screw, built at the origin on its datum — seating plane z = 0,
// shank down — with its material set there, so the relief moves with it.
screw = fastener.shcs(d, screwLength);
screw.material = material.withDisplacement(steelMat,
                                          thread.maleRelief(d, pitchVal, 0.0, 0.0 - screwLength));
screw.color = thread.reliefColor(steelColor,
                                 thread.maleRelief(d, pitchVal, 0.0, 0.0 - screwLength), pitchVal);

// The plate, drilled at the thread's basic minor diameter and tapped through
// its whole thickness.
plate = max(box([-6.0, -6.0, 0.0], [6.0, 6.0, plateT]),
            thread.minorDia(d, pitchVal) / 2.0 - length(p.xy));
plate.material = material.withDisplacement(aluminumMat,
                                          thread.femaleRelief(d, pitchVal, plateT, 0.0));
plate.color = thread.reliefColor(aluminumColor,
                                 thread.femaleRelief(d, pitchVal, plateT, 0.0), pitchVal);

// A shorter screw for the joint, seated six millimetres above the plate so
// the thread between its head and the plate shows.
backedOut = 6.0;
stub = fastener.shcs(d, 16.0);
stub.material = material.withDisplacement(steelMat,
                                        thread.maleRelief(d, pitchVal, 0.0, -16.0));
stub.color = thread.reliefColor(steelColor, thread.maleRelief(d, pitchVal, 0.0, -16.0), pitchVal);

looseScrew = transform.translate(screw, [-18.0, 0.0, screwLength]);
tappedPlate = remap(plate, [p.x, p.y, p.z]);
jointPlate = transform.translate(plate, [18.0, 0.0, 0.0]);
jointScrew = transform.translate(stub, [18.0, 0.0, plateT + backedOut]);

return looseScrew, tappedPlate, jointPlate, jointScrew;
